# Line endings are load-bearing in this repository, not a style preference.
#
# `build.py` applies `patches/` with GNU `patch` against a Chromium checkout whose sources are LF.
# Git's default on Windows here is `core.autocrlf=true`, so without this file a fresh clone would
# materialise every `.patch` with CRLF line endings and hand `patch` hunks whose every line carries a
# trailing CR. The local build tree happens to hold LF copies because the files were written that way,
# so the hazard is invisible until CI checks the repository out -- and no CI build has ever applied a
# `patches/veil/` patch (Stage 4 published a zero-patch release). Pin it rather than discover it.
#
# `patches/series` is extensionless and is read line by line, so it is pinned by name.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.patch text eol=lf
patches/series text eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
*.7z binary
*.gz binary
*.tar binary
*.xz binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.pdb binary
